WEBVTT

1
00:01:55.566 --> 00:01:57.632
         (BOTH YELLING)

2
00:02:10.146 --> 00:02:12.180
        (CROWD CHEERING)

3
00:02:13.049 --> 00:02:15.167
           Well struck.

4
00:02:15.219 --> 00:02:16.852
        Well struck. dog.

5
00:02:21.208 --> 00:02:22.740
             Did you like that?

6
00:02:22.810 --> 00:02:24.709
 It was well struck.
 Your Grace.

7
00:02:24.778 --> 00:02:27.212
            I already said
            it was well struck.

8
00:02:28.248 --> 00:02:30.165
 Yes. Your Grace.

9
00:02:37.858 --> 00:02:39.023
     Who's next?

10
00:02:39.092 --> 00:02:40.225
 HERALD: Lothor Brune.

11
00:02:40.293 --> 00:02:43.495
 freerider in the service
 of Lord Baelish.

12
00:02:43.564 --> 00:02:46.731
  Ser Dontos the Red
  of House Hollard.

13
00:02:49.670 --> 00:02:52.454
  Ser Dontos the Red
  of House Hollard!

14
00:02:52.522 --> 00:02:53.955
             DONTOS: Here I am.

15
00:02:54.041 --> 00:02:56.041
                Here I am.

16
00:03:02.182 --> 00:03:03.865
     Sorry. Your Grace.

17
00:03:04.801 --> 00:03:06.701
     My deepest apologies.

18
00:03:06.770 --> 00:03:08.369
        JOFFREY: Are you drunk?
             No.

19
00:03:09.039 --> 00:03:11.190
 No. No. Your Grace.

20
00:03:11.258 --> 00:03:12.791
 I had two cups of wine.

21
00:03:12.859 --> 00:03:13.892
                      Two cups?

22
00:03:13.944 --> 00:03:16.411
 That's not much at all.

23
00:03:16.480 --> 00:03:18.579
 Please. have another cup.

24
00:03:18.649 --> 00:03:20.114
 Are you sure. Your Grace?

25
00:03:20.201 --> 00:03:22.501
 Yes. To celebrate
 my name day.

26
00:03:22.570 --> 00:03:25.002
      Have two.
      Have as much as you like.

27
00:03:26.322 --> 00:03:27.906
 I would be honored.
 Your Grace.

28
00:03:29.560 --> 00:03:33.261
   Ser Meryn. help Ser Dontos
   celebrate my name day.

29
00:03:33.329 --> 00:03:34.746
            See that
            he drinks his fill.

30
00:03:37.317 --> 00:03:38.333
         (CROWD GASPS)

31
00:03:50.130 --> 00:03:52.314
                (GURGLING)

32
00:03:53.066 --> 00:03:55.400
                    You can't.

33
00:03:55.469 --> 00:03:57.084
   What did you say?

34
00:03:58.421 --> 00:04:00.255
           Did you say I can't?

35
00:04:00.323 --> 00:04:01.890
  I only meant

36
00:04:01.959 --> 00:04:04.876
 it would be bad luck
 to kill a man
 on your name day.

37
00:04:04.945 --> 00:04:07.562
      What kind of stupid
      peasant's superstition...

38
00:04:07.631 --> 00:04:09.197
 HOUND:
 The girl is right.

39
00:04:09.266 --> 00:04:12.450
  What a man sows
  on his name day.
  he reaps all year.

40
00:04:12.519 --> 00:04:14.218
 (MEN LAUGHING)
   (WINE POURING)

41
00:04:14.288 --> 00:04:15.820
           (SIGHS)

42
00:04:15.889 --> 00:04:17.389
      Take him away.

43
00:04:17.457 --> 00:04:19.507
   I'll have him killed
   tomorrow. the fool.

44
00:04:20.994 --> 00:04:23.311
       (CROWD MURMURING)

45
00:04:23.379 --> 00:04:26.715
               He is a fool.
               You're so clever
               to see it.

46
00:04:26.784 --> 00:04:29.384
       He'll make a much better
       fool than a knight.

47
00:04:29.453 --> 00:04:32.454
    He doesn't deserve
    the mercy of a quick death.

48
00:04:34.174 --> 00:04:36.992
 Did you hear my lady.
 Ser Dontos?

49
00:04:37.060 --> 00:04:40.145
 From this day.
 you'll be my new fool.

50
00:04:40.197 --> 00:04:42.397
     Thank you. Your Grace.

51
00:04:42.465 --> 00:04:45.633
        And you. my lady.
        thank you.

52
00:04:45.702 --> 00:04:47.335
        TYRION: Beloved nephew.

53
00:04:54.778 --> 00:04:57.412
      We looked for you
      on the battlefield.

54
00:04:59.482 --> 00:05:02.049
 You were nowhere
 to be found.

55
00:05:03.520 --> 00:05:05.653
 I've been here.
 ruling the kingdoms.

56
00:05:05.722 --> 00:05:08.373
       What a fine job
       you've done.

57
00:05:09.410 --> 00:05:10.525
          Look at you.

58
00:05:12.112 --> 00:05:14.212
 More beautiful than ever.

59
00:05:14.281 --> 00:05:16.014
 And you!

60
00:05:16.082 --> 00:05:18.349
 You're going to be
 bigger than the Hound.

61
00:05:18.402 --> 00:05:20.802
       but much better looking.
                       (LAUGHS)

62
00:05:20.871 --> 00:05:22.820
            This one
            doesn't like me.

63
00:05:22.889 --> 00:05:24.739
     Can't imagine why.

64
00:05:24.825 --> 00:05:26.057
        We heard you were dead.

65
00:05:26.126 --> 00:05:27.308
    I'm glad
    you're not dead.

66
00:05:28.362 --> 00:05:30.996
            Me. too. dear.
            Death is so boring.

67
00:05:31.065 --> 00:05:35.283
        especially now.
        with so much excitement
        in the world.

68
00:05:35.352 --> 00:05:36.701
       My lady.
       I'm sorry for your loss.

69
00:05:38.554 --> 00:05:39.854
     Her loss?

70
00:05:39.923 --> 00:05:41.856
 Her father was
 a confessed traitor.

71
00:05:41.925 --> 00:05:43.925
       But still her father.

72
00:05:43.994 --> 00:05:46.227
  Surely. having so recently
  lost your own beloved father.
  you can sympathize.

73
00:05:51.602 --> 00:05:53.452
 My father was a traitor.

74
00:05:53.520 --> 00:05:55.803
 My mother and brother
 are traitors. too.

75
00:05:55.872 --> 00:05:57.973
 I am loyal to my
 beloved Joffrey.

76
00:05:59.810 --> 00:06:01.959
             Of course you are.

77
00:06:03.997 --> 00:06:07.832
     Well. enjoy your name day.
     Your Grace.

78
00:06:07.901 --> 00:06:09.583
            Wish I could stay
            and celebrate.

79
00:06:09.652 --> 00:06:12.470
     but there is work
     to be done.

80
00:06:12.539 --> 00:06:14.539
              What work?

81
00:06:14.608 --> 00:06:16.574
         Why are you here?

82
00:06:20.297 --> 00:06:24.666
 PYCELLE: A raven
 arrived from the citadel
 this morning. Your Grace.

83
00:06:24.734 --> 00:06:25.933
      (BIRD SQUAWKING)

84
00:06:26.002 --> 00:06:27.602
 The conclave has met.

85
00:06:27.671 --> 00:06:31.773
 considered reports
 from maesters all over
 the Seven Kingdoms.

86
00:06:31.841 --> 00:06:34.676
 and declared
 this great summer

87
00:06:34.744 --> 00:06:37.295
   done at last.

88
00:06:37.347 --> 00:06:40.448
             The longest summer
             in living memory.

89
00:06:40.516 --> 00:06:43.784
     The peasants say.
     a long summer means
     an even longer winter.

90
00:06:43.853 --> 00:06:45.620
         PYCELLE:
         A common superstition.

91
00:06:45.689 --> 00:06:48.089
 LITTLEFINGER:
 We have enough wheat
 for a five-year winter.

92
00:06:48.158 --> 00:06:50.992
        If it lasts any longer.

93
00:06:51.061 --> 00:06:53.028
     we'll have fewer peasants.

94
00:06:53.096 --> 00:06:56.497
 The city's drowning
 in refugees. Your Grace.
 fleeing the war.

95
00:06:56.566 --> 00:06:57.866
 We have nowhere
 to house them.

96
00:06:57.934 --> 00:06:59.651
 And with winter coming.
 it'll only get worse.

97
00:06:59.720 --> 00:07:03.020
    You command the city watch.
    do you not. Lord Slynt?

98
00:07:04.324 --> 00:07:06.124
 I do. Your Grace.

99
00:07:06.192 --> 00:07:08.192
         And are you not a lord
         at my command?

100
00:07:08.262 --> 00:07:11.863
 I owe my title and lands
 to your generosity.
 Your Grace.

101
00:07:11.931 --> 00:07:14.465
             Then do your job.
             Shut the gates
             to the peasants.

102
00:07:14.534 --> 00:07:17.418
      They belong in the field.
      not our capital.

103
00:07:17.487 --> 00:07:19.087
 Yes. Your Grace.

104
00:07:19.156 --> 00:07:20.488
    (TYRION WHISTLING TUNE)

105
00:07:25.828 --> 00:07:26.895
     Don't get up.

106
00:07:28.348 --> 00:07:31.933
 More ravishing than ever.
 big sister.

107
00:07:33.453 --> 00:07:35.920
      War agrees with you.

108
00:07:35.989 --> 00:07:38.506
   Forgive the interruption.
   Carry on.

109
00:07:40.360 --> 00:07:42.376
       What are you doing here?

110
00:07:42.445 --> 00:07:45.764
 It's been
 a remarkable journey.

111
00:07:45.832 --> 00:07:48.849
 I pissed off
 the edge of the Wall.

112
00:07:49.886 --> 00:07:51.786
 I slept in a sky cell.

113
00:07:51.872 --> 00:07:54.072
       I fought with
       the hill tribes.

114
00:07:54.141 --> 00:07:55.674
    So many adventures.

115
00:07:56.893 --> 00:07:59.544
 so much to be thankful for.

116
00:07:59.596 --> 00:08:03.497
     What are you doing here?
     This is the small council.

117
00:08:03.567 --> 00:08:06.801
 Yes. well. I do believe
 the Hand of the King
 is welcome

118
00:08:06.869 --> 00:08:08.303
 at all small
 council meetings.

119
00:08:08.372 --> 00:08:10.104
              Our father is
              Hand of the King.

120
00:08:10.190 --> 00:08:13.191
 Yes. but in his absence...

121
00:08:20.550 --> 00:08:22.884
          VARYS: Your father
          has named Lord Tyrion

122
00:08:22.953 --> 00:08:25.503
               to serve as hand
               in his stead
               while he fights.

123
00:08:25.572 --> 00:08:27.989
          Out! All of you out!

124
00:08:32.929 --> 00:08:35.563
 I would like to know
 how you tricked Father
 into this.

125
00:08:35.632 --> 00:08:37.532
            If I were capable
            of tricking Father.

126
00:08:37.601 --> 00:08:39.801
              I'd be emperor of
              the world by now.

127
00:08:39.870 --> 00:08:42.203
 You brought this
 on yourself.

128
00:08:42.272 --> 00:08:43.304
             I've done nothing.

129
00:08:43.390 --> 00:08:45.223
 Quite right.
 you did nothing

130
00:08:45.292 --> 00:08:47.525
 when your son called
 for Ned Stark's head.

131
00:08:47.594 --> 00:08:49.543
 Now the entire North
 has risen up against us.

132
00:08:49.612 --> 00:08:50.811
            I tried to stop it.

133
00:08:50.880 --> 00:08:52.413
 Did you? You failed.

134
00:08:52.482 --> 00:08:55.333
 That bit of theater
 will haunt our family
 for a generation.

135
00:08:55.402 --> 00:08:56.834
         Robb Stark is a child.

136
00:08:56.904 --> 00:08:59.871
 Who's won every battle
 he's fought.

137
00:08:59.939 --> 00:09:01.723
 Do you understand
 we're losing the war?

138
00:09:01.792 --> 00:09:03.591
               What do you know
               about warfare?

139
00:09:03.660 --> 00:09:04.859
  Nothing.

140
00:09:04.928 --> 00:09:06.694
 But I know people.

141
00:09:06.763 --> 00:09:08.830
 And I know that our
 enemies hate each other

142
00:09:08.899 --> 00:09:11.449
 almost as much as
 they hate us.

143
00:09:16.089 --> 00:09:17.488
               Joffrey is king.

144
00:09:17.557 --> 00:09:19.423
 Joffrey is king.

145
00:09:19.492 --> 00:09:21.159
                 You are here
                 to advise him.

146
00:09:21.228 --> 00:09:23.328
 I'm only here
 to advise him.

147
00:09:23.397 --> 00:09:25.496
 And if the king
 listens to what I say.

148
00:09:25.565 --> 00:09:29.067
 the king might just get
 his Uncle Jaime back.

149
00:09:30.904 --> 00:09:32.337
                         How?

150
00:09:32.406 --> 00:09:33.971
 You love your children.

151
00:09:34.040 --> 00:09:37.074
 It's your
 one redeeming quality.
 That and your cheekbones.

152
00:09:38.478 --> 00:09:41.413
 The Starks love
 their children as well.

153
00:09:41.481 --> 00:09:43.698
  And we have
  two of them.
                     One.

154
00:09:45.602 --> 00:09:46.868
     One?

155
00:09:46.936 --> 00:09:48.403
           Arya. little animal.
           she disappeared.

156
00:09:48.472 --> 00:09:51.489
 Disappeared? What.
 in a puff of smoke?

157
00:09:53.626 --> 00:09:56.561
 We had three Starks
 to trade.

158
00:09:56.629 --> 00:09:59.263
 You chopped one's head off
 and let another escape.

159
00:10:00.317 --> 00:10:02.317
 Father will be furious.

160
00:10:03.486 --> 00:10:04.952
 It must be odd for you

161
00:10:07.524 --> 00:10:09.924
 to be
 the disappointing child.

162
00:10:17.617 --> 00:10:21.252
      LEADRANACH:
      My lord. may the old gods
      watch over your brother

163
00:10:21.320 --> 00:10:23.971
     and all our Northern sons.

164
00:10:24.041 --> 00:10:27.875
     The walls of my holdfast
     will not stand the winter.

165
00:10:27.944 --> 00:10:32.080
           The stones were last
           mortared in the time
           of King Aerys.

166
00:10:32.149 --> 00:10:34.449
               and I'm afraid
               the masons today

167
00:10:34.518 --> 00:10:36.751
        are not fit to carry
        their fathers' hammers.

168
00:10:38.055 --> 00:10:39.587
              When I was a boy.

169
00:10:39.656 --> 00:10:42.357
         I remember seeing them
         put up a new tower

170
00:10:42.426 --> 00:10:45.060
            at Torrhen's Square
            in a summer.

171
00:10:45.128 --> 00:10:47.095
          Men worked back then.

172
00:10:47.164 --> 00:10:52.483
      Today. my holdfast
      looks like it was built
      by drunk children.

173
00:10:52.552 --> 00:10:57.271
       At night you can hear
       the wind howling
       through the gaps.

174
00:10:57.340 --> 00:10:59.006
      Gods forbid it rains.

175
00:10:59.075 --> 00:11:01.909
     Why. I might as well
     sleep beneath a waterfall.

176
00:11:01.978 --> 00:11:06.981
  Maintenance of a holdfast
  generally falls to the lord
  of that holdfast.

177
00:11:07.067 --> 00:11:08.633
          Generally. yes.

178
00:11:08.701 --> 00:11:12.036
     but I've sent
     all the young men off
     to fight Robb Stark's war.

179
00:11:12.104 --> 00:11:15.223
 King Robb.
 And it's not his war.

180
00:11:15.292 --> 00:11:17.158
 He didn't choose it.

181
00:11:17.243 --> 00:11:20.778
      Maybe not. my lord.
      but he called in his
      banners and took the men.

182
00:11:20.847 --> 00:11:22.497
 Joffrey killed my father.

183
00:11:23.133 --> 00:11:24.999
 your liege lord.

184
00:11:25.068 --> 00:11:27.468
 Do you remember
 your vows. ser?

185
00:11:27.537 --> 00:11:29.403
          Of course I remember!

186
00:11:29.472 --> 00:11:32.507
       We can spare four masons
       for a week. my lord.

187
00:11:32.575 --> 00:11:35.593
        Will that be sufficient
        to repair your walls?

188
00:11:35.662 --> 00:11:37.695
          I believe it will.

189
00:11:43.903 --> 00:11:47.472
        We didn't want him here
        all day. did we?

190
00:11:47.541 --> 00:11:50.508
 I didn't like the way
 he was talking about Robb.

191
00:11:50.577 --> 00:11:52.243
                    Nor did I.

192
00:11:54.697 --> 00:11:57.598
   But listening to people
   you'd rather not listen to

193
00:11:57.667 --> 00:12:01.569
     is one of your
     responsibilities
     as Lord of Winterfell.

194
00:12:01.637 --> 00:12:03.271
 (BRAN SIGHS)

195
00:12:05.124 --> 00:12:06.908
 Lord Portan.

196
00:12:06.977 --> 00:12:09.877
      My lord. may the old gods
      watch over your brother

197
00:12:09.946 --> 00:12:11.646
                 and all our
                 Northern sons.

198
00:12:13.800 --> 00:12:15.900
       (HEAVY BREATHING)

199
00:12:22.275 --> 00:12:24.041
               (WINGS FLAPPING)
 (BIRD SQUAWKING)

200
00:13:00.630 --> 00:13:04.032
          Boil this for an hour
          and drink the tea.

201
00:13:05.134 --> 00:13:07.535
                Makes all your
                pain go away.

202
00:13:07.604 --> 00:13:09.103
 BRAN:
 Don't have any pain.

203
00:13:10.257 --> 00:13:11.722
             Lucky for you.

204
00:13:12.942 --> 00:13:14.275
              That way.

205
00:13:17.513 --> 00:13:19.813
 You've been having
 those dreams again.

206
00:13:19.882 --> 00:13:21.549
           BRAN: I don't dream.

207
00:13:21.618 --> 00:13:23.150
        Everyone dreams.

208
00:13:23.220 --> 00:13:24.785
            I don't.

209
00:13:26.189 --> 00:13:28.205
     Heard some of the men
     talking about the comet.

210
00:13:28.991 --> 00:13:30.524
     They say it's an omen.

211
00:13:30.593 --> 00:13:34.027
    They say it means Robb
    will win a great victory
    in the South.

212
00:13:34.096 --> 00:13:35.547
  Did they?

213
00:13:37.651 --> 00:13:41.185
 I heard some other fools say
 it's Lannister Red.

214
00:13:41.254 --> 00:13:44.405
 Means the Lannisters
 will rule all Seven
 Kingdoms before long.

215
00:13:44.491 --> 00:13:47.959
 Heard a stable boy say
 it's the color of blood

216
00:13:48.027 --> 00:13:50.194
 to mark the death
 of your father.

217
00:13:54.150 --> 00:13:57.351
 The stars don't
 fall for men.

218
00:13:57.420 --> 00:13:59.854
                Red comet means
                one thing. boy.

219
00:14:01.157 --> 00:14:02.556
                       Dragons.

220
00:14:04.627 --> 00:14:07.361
 The dragons are all dead.

221
00:14:07.430 --> 00:14:09.763
 They've been dead
 for centuries.

222
00:14:42.666 --> 00:14:44.231
              (SHRIEKS)

223
00:14:46.770 --> 00:14:48.052
                 Mmm.

224
00:14:53.143 --> 00:14:55.743
      What did your brother say
      about them. Khaleesi?

225
00:14:55.812 --> 00:14:57.478
 He said they ate meat.

226
00:14:57.547 --> 00:15:01.282
             He didn't tell you
             what kind of meat?

227
00:15:01.350 --> 00:15:04.218
 My brother didn't know
 anything about dragons.

228
00:15:04.287 --> 00:15:07.288
 He didn't know
 anything about anything.

229
00:15:12.395 --> 00:15:13.394
               Eh.

230
00:15:16.649 --> 00:15:17.631
      (WHINNIES)

231
00:15:20.954 --> 00:15:22.420
       (WOMEN MURMURING)

232
00:15:41.257 --> 00:15:43.224
              She was Drogo's
              first gift to me.

233
00:15:44.377 --> 00:15:46.010
      I remember.

234
00:15:48.198 --> 00:15:50.764
               I promised
               to protect them.

235
00:15:50.833 --> 00:15:53.100
           Promised them
           their enemies
           would die screaming.

236
00:15:53.169 --> 00:15:55.769
             How do I make
             starvation scream?

237
00:15:55.838 --> 00:15:58.372
    A trick I never learned.
    I'm afraid.

238
00:16:00.543 --> 00:16:02.710
              Does it ever end?

239
00:16:02.778 --> 00:16:04.645
      This is further east
      than I've ever been.

240
00:16:04.714 --> 00:16:07.781
      But. yes. Khaleesi.
      everything ends.
      even the Red Waste.

241
00:16:07.867 --> 00:16:10.335
          And you're sure
          there's no other way?

242
00:16:10.403 --> 00:16:13.037
  If we go south
  to the land of
  the Lhazareen.

243
00:16:13.105 --> 00:16:15.606
 the Lamb Men will kill us
 and take your dragons.

244
00:16:15.675 --> 00:16:17.475
 If we go west to
 the Dothraki Sea.

245
00:16:17.544 --> 00:16:21.179
 the first khalasar we meet
 will kill us and take
 your dragons.

246
00:16:21.231 --> 00:16:23.647
               No one will
               take my dragons.

247
00:16:25.001 --> 00:16:27.668
 They are too weak to fight.

248
00:16:27.737 --> 00:16:29.804
 as are your people.

249
00:16:29.873 --> 00:16:31.989
 You must be their strength.

250
00:16:33.092 --> 00:16:35.026
               As you are mine.

251
00:16:39.015 --> 00:16:40.447
             (SPEAKS DOTHRAKI)

252
00:17:11.831 --> 00:17:13.264
            (SPEAKS DOTHRAKI)

253
00:17:22.208 --> 00:17:23.740
                       Rakharo.

254
00:17:32.434 --> 00:17:34.301
                You never have.

255
00:17:39.642 --> 00:17:42.743
 This is bad time to start.

256
00:17:56.559 --> 00:17:58.459
 (HORSE WHINNIES)

257
00:18:19.649 --> 00:18:21.516
         (WIND HOWLING)

258
00:18:39.135 --> 00:18:41.101
 Having a rough time of it?

259
00:18:41.170 --> 00:18:42.703
      Nothing's killed me yet.

260
00:18:42.772 --> 00:18:44.104
             GRENN: Your arse
             killed the sledge.

261
00:18:44.173 --> 00:18:45.439
      You offered me a ride.

262
00:18:45.508 --> 00:18:48.459
            I just wanted you
            to shut up about
            your damn blisters.

263
00:19:02.759 --> 00:19:05.525
          I was born in a place
          like this.

264
00:19:05.594 --> 00:19:08.495
           Later. I fell
           on hard times.

265
00:19:10.299 --> 00:19:12.032
 SAMWELL: Are those girls?

266
00:19:12.101 --> 00:19:14.535
           DOLOROUS EDD:
           Craster's daughters.

267
00:19:14.604 --> 00:19:17.905
          I haven't seen a girl
          in six months.

268
00:19:17.973 --> 00:19:20.674
            I'd keep on
            not seeing them
            if I were you.

269
00:19:20.743 --> 00:19:22.910
  What. he don't like people
  messing with his daughters?

270
00:19:22.979 --> 00:19:25.579
        He don't like people
        messing with his wives.

271
00:19:28.067 --> 00:19:31.435
     He marries his daughters.
     and they give him
     more daughters.

272
00:19:31.504 --> 00:19:34.121
     And on and on it goes.

273
00:19:34.190 --> 00:19:36.574
                   That's foul.
           It's beyond foul.

274
00:19:36.643 --> 00:19:40.478
        All the other wildlings
        for a hundred leagues
        have disappeared.

275
00:19:40.546 --> 00:19:42.513
          Craster's still here.

276
00:19:42.582 --> 00:19:44.998
            He must be doing
            something right.

277
00:19:46.836 --> 00:19:48.535
   What happens
   to the boys?

278
00:19:48.604 --> 00:19:49.737
           Hmm?

279
00:19:49.805 --> 00:19:52.172
                 He marries
                 his daughters.

280
00:19:52.241 --> 00:19:54.475
           What does he do
           with his sons?

281
00:19:57.296 --> 00:20:01.081
 He said he planned
 to stop here on his way
 to the Frostfangs.

282
00:20:01.150 --> 00:20:02.750
  People make all
  sorts of plans.

283
00:20:02.818 --> 00:20:06.186
 I haven't seen Benjen Stark
 in three years.

284
00:20:06.255 --> 00:20:07.688
  Haven't missed him.

285
00:20:07.757 --> 00:20:11.575
              Always treated me
              like scum.

286
00:20:11.644 --> 00:20:14.461
          Haven't had any good
          wine for a long time.

287
00:20:14.530 --> 00:20:17.381
            You Southerners
            make good wine.
            I'll give you that.

288
00:20:17.449 --> 00:20:19.400
         We're not Southerners.

289
00:20:19.469 --> 00:20:21.068
 Who's this little girl?

290
00:20:22.705 --> 00:20:25.438
 You're prettier
 than half my daughters.

291
00:20:25.507 --> 00:20:28.825
 You got a nice wet twat
 between your legs?

292
00:20:28.895 --> 00:20:30.644
 What's your name?

293
00:20:30.713 --> 00:20:32.763
               Jon Snow.
 Snow. eh?

294
00:20:32.831 --> 00:20:35.699
         Listen to me. bastard.

295
00:20:35.768 --> 00:20:39.703
 All you lot from
 south of the Wall.
 you're Southerners.

296
00:20:39.772 --> 00:20:43.674
   But now you're
   in the North.
   the real North.

297
00:20:43.743 --> 00:20:44.959
 The lad meant no harm.

298
00:20:46.629 --> 00:20:50.081
 I catch that
 pretty little bastard
 talking to my daughters...

299
00:20:50.149 --> 00:20:54.051
             No one will talk
             to your daughters.
             you have my word.

300
00:20:54.120 --> 00:20:57.154
           Now. sit down
           and shut your mouth.

301
00:21:00.242 --> 00:21:02.426
          You bring any of that
          good wine with you?

302
00:21:02.495 --> 00:21:04.161
          We did.

303
00:21:04.229 --> 00:21:06.831
     We passed through
     six villages
     on the way here.

304
00:21:06.899 --> 00:21:08.749
 All six were abandoned.

305
00:21:09.802 --> 00:21:11.736
 Where have all
 the wildlings gone?

306
00:21:11.804 --> 00:21:15.572
              I could tell you.
              but I'm thirsty.

307
00:21:15.641 --> 00:21:17.675
 MORMONT: There's
 a barrel of Dornish wine
 on the sledge.

308
00:21:17.743 --> 00:21:18.992
 Bring it in here.

309
00:21:19.061 --> 00:21:20.444
           MAN: Yes. Commander.

310
00:21:20.513 --> 00:21:23.497
      CRASTER: You want to know
      where they've all gone?

311
00:21:23.566 --> 00:21:27.568
             North. to join up
             with Mance Rayder.

312
00:21:28.988 --> 00:21:31.004
  Your old friend.

313
00:21:31.073 --> 00:21:33.340
 He's no friend of mine.

314
00:21:33.408 --> 00:21:36.710
 He broke his vows.
 betrayed his brothers.

315
00:21:36.779 --> 00:21:37.828
                  Aye.

316
00:21:37.896 --> 00:21:40.998
        But once he was
        just a poor black crow.

317
00:21:41.067 --> 00:21:43.900
          And now he's
          King-beyond-the-Wall.

318
00:21:43.969 --> 00:21:46.403
 He's been calling
 himself that for years.

319
00:21:46.472 --> 00:21:50.073
 What's he king of?
 A frozen lake somewhere?

320
00:21:51.577 --> 00:21:53.610
      That's a good-looking ax.

321
00:21:53.679 --> 00:21:55.646
                  Fresh forged?

322
00:21:57.783 --> 00:22:00.250
                Give it here.

323
00:22:00.319 --> 00:22:02.553
 You'll have another one
 made at Castle Black.

324
00:22:02.622 --> 00:22:04.555
       Here.

325
00:22:05.991 --> 00:22:08.125
                  That's some
                  lovely steel.

326
00:22:12.048 --> 00:22:15.015
         You want to know what
         Mance Rayder is doing?

327
00:22:15.084 --> 00:22:17.234
             Gathering an army.

328
00:22:17.303 --> 00:22:20.871
      What I hear. he's already
      got more men than any of
      your Southern Kings.

329
00:22:20.939 --> 00:22:24.208
 And where does he plan
 marching this army?

330
00:22:24.276 --> 00:22:27.194
        When you're all the way
        north. there's only one
        direction to go.

331
00:22:29.598 --> 00:22:34.201
 These are bad times to be
 living alone in the wild.

332
00:22:34.270 --> 00:22:36.303
 The cold winds are rising.

333
00:22:37.573 --> 00:22:41.008
        Let them come.
        My roots are sunk deep.

334
00:22:42.628 --> 00:22:44.595
                          Wife.

335
00:22:44.664 --> 00:22:48.982
            tell the Lord Crow
            how content we are.

336
00:22:49.051 --> 00:22:51.018
    This is our place.

337
00:22:51.086 --> 00:22:52.937
 Our husband keeps us safe.

338
00:22:52.989 --> 00:22:55.990
 Better to live free
 than die a slave.

339
00:22:58.544 --> 00:23:01.512
 CRASTER: Don't it make you
 jealous. old man.

340
00:23:01.580 --> 00:23:03.580
    to see me with
    all these young wives

341
00:23:03.649 --> 00:23:06.917
    and you with no one
    to warm your bed?

342
00:23:06.985 --> 00:23:09.003
      We chose different paths.

343
00:23:09.088 --> 00:23:13.257
 Aye. and you chose the path
 with no one but boys on it.

344
00:23:15.310 --> 00:23:18.278
 You'll be wanting to sleep
 beneath my roof. I suppose.

345
00:23:18.347 --> 00:23:20.447
        and eat me out of pigs.

346
00:23:20.516 --> 00:23:22.382
 A roof would be welcome.

347
00:23:22.451 --> 00:23:23.884
 It's been hard riding.

348
00:23:23.953 --> 00:23:27.204
 We've brought our own food
 and good steel for you.

349
00:23:29.842 --> 00:23:32.543
 Any man lays a hand
 on one of my wives.

350
00:23:33.412 --> 00:23:35.245
             he loses the hand.

351
00:23:37.450 --> 00:23:41.218
         And I see this one
         staring too long.

352
00:23:41.286 --> 00:23:44.454
       I might just
       gouge his eyes out.

353
00:23:44.523 --> 00:23:47.725
 Your roof. your rules.

354
00:23:59.238 --> 00:24:00.671
            (GRUNTS)

355
00:24:00.739 --> 00:24:02.406
                 Who am I?

356
00:24:03.209 --> 00:24:04.474
                  Who am I?

357
00:24:05.411 --> 00:24:06.610
       Lord Commander.

358
00:24:06.679 --> 00:24:08.578
               And who are you?

359
00:24:08.647 --> 00:24:09.780
          Jon Snow.

360
00:24:09.849 --> 00:24:11.248
                 Who are you?

361
00:24:12.718 --> 00:24:14.618
     Your steward.

362
00:24:14.687 --> 00:24:16.687
                You want to
                lead one day?

363
00:24:19.758 --> 00:24:21.959
                 Then learn
                 how to follow.

364
00:24:35.825 --> 00:24:37.490
         (MAN PANTING)

365
00:24:39.494 --> 00:24:44.164
    MELISANDRE: Lord of Light.
    come to us in our darkness.

366
00:24:44.233 --> 00:24:48.218
              We offer you
              these false gods.

367
00:24:48.271 --> 00:24:51.104
            Take them and cast
            your light upon us.

368
00:24:52.908 --> 00:24:57.010
          for the night is dark
          and full of terrors.

369
00:24:57.079 --> 00:25:00.246
   MEN: For the night is dark
   and full of terrors.

370
00:25:02.634 --> 00:25:04.568
         MELISANDRE:
         After the long summer.

371
00:25:04.636 --> 00:25:07.505
            darkness will fall
            heavy on the world.

372
00:25:07.573 --> 00:25:10.257
          The stars will bleed.

373
00:25:10.325 --> 00:25:12.860
     We need to stop her.

374
00:25:12.928 --> 00:25:16.714
      MELISANDRE:
      The cold breath of winter
      will freeze the seas...

375
00:25:16.782 --> 00:25:18.115
    Not now.

376
00:25:18.184 --> 00:25:20.918
       ...and the dead
       shall rise in the North.

377
00:25:22.638 --> 00:25:26.272
 All you men were named
 in the light of the Seven!

378
00:25:26.341 --> 00:25:29.426
 Is this how you treat
 the gods of your fathers?

379
00:25:29.478 --> 00:25:34.047
 Are you so eager to
 spit on your ancestors?

380
00:25:42.741 --> 00:25:45.092
   You smell of fear.

381
00:25:45.160 --> 00:25:49.129
 fear and piss
 and old bones.

382
00:25:50.649 --> 00:25:52.199
 Do you want to stop me?

383
00:25:56.856 --> 00:25:58.588
                    Stop me.

384
00:26:11.586 --> 00:26:13.286
 In the ancient books.
 it's written

385
00:26:13.355 --> 00:26:17.057
 that a warrior will draw
 a burning sword
 from the fire.

386
00:26:18.327 --> 00:26:21.395
 And that sword
 shall be Lightbringer.

387
00:26:26.352 --> 00:26:29.820
 Stannis Baratheon.

388
00:26:29.888 --> 00:26:32.389
 Warrior of Light.

389
00:26:32.458 --> 00:26:34.208
 your sword awaits you.

390
00:26:55.731 --> 00:26:57.463
         (MEN CHEERING)

391
00:27:05.224 --> 00:27:07.941
    MEN: Lord.
    cast your light upon us!

392
00:27:09.645 --> 00:27:12.812
          MELISANDRE:
          For the night is dark
          and full of terrors.

393
00:27:15.967 --> 00:27:19.085
          For the night is dark
          and full of terror.

394
00:27:46.381 --> 00:27:49.983
 This woman will lead him
 into a war he cannot win.

395
00:27:50.069 --> 00:27:51.668
           Stannis is our king.

396
00:27:51.737 --> 00:27:53.170
                We follow
                where he leads.

397
00:27:53.239 --> 00:27:55.772
               even if we don't
               like the path.
         King.

398
00:27:55.841 --> 00:27:59.943
 Since that boar killed
 his brother. every lord
 wants a coronation.

399
00:28:00.012 --> 00:28:02.212
      I don't serve the others.
      I serve Stannis.

400
00:28:02.280 --> 00:28:03.914
      As do I.

401
00:28:03.982 --> 00:28:08.802
 but loyal service
 means telling hard truths.

402
00:28:08.870 --> 00:28:11.671
       He's surrounded by
       fools and fanatics.

403
00:28:12.975 --> 00:28:15.825
 but he trusts you. Davos.

404
00:28:15.894 --> 00:28:18.478
      If you tell him
      the truth...

405
00:28:20.298 --> 00:28:21.948
              What's the truth?

406
00:28:34.913 --> 00:28:38.181
 MATTHOS: "And I declare upon
 the honor of my house that
 my beloved brother Robert..."

407
00:28:38.250 --> 00:28:40.884
             He wasn't my
             beloved brother.

408
00:28:40.952 --> 00:28:42.986
           I didn't love him.
           He didn't love me.

409
00:28:43.055 --> 00:28:44.871
     A harmless courtesy.
     Your Grace.

410
00:28:44.957 --> 00:28:46.022
            A lie. Take it out.

411
00:28:49.228 --> 00:28:51.678
 "That my brother Robert
 left no trueborn heirs.

412
00:28:51.747 --> 00:28:53.514
 "the boy Joffrey.
 the boy Tommen.

413
00:28:53.582 --> 00:28:55.782
 "and the girl Myrcella
 being born of incest

414
00:28:55.851 --> 00:28:58.918
 "between Cersei Lannister
 and her brother
 Jaime Lannister.

415
00:28:58.987 --> 00:29:01.755
 "By right of birth..."
           Jaime Lannister.
           the Kingslayer.

416
00:29:01.824 --> 00:29:03.156
         Call him what he is.

417
00:29:05.294 --> 00:29:07.661
 "And her brother
 Jaime Lannister.
 the Kingslayer."

418
00:29:07.729 --> 00:29:11.031
 "By right of birth and blood.
 I do this day lay claim..."

419
00:29:11.099 --> 00:29:14.001
           STANNIS: Make it
           Ser Jaime Lannister.
           the Kingslayer.

420
00:29:14.069 --> 00:29:16.135
      Whatever else he is.
      the man's still a knight.

421
00:29:16.205 --> 00:29:18.539
 "Ser Jaime Lannister.
 the Kingslayer.

422
00:29:18.607 --> 00:29:20.857
  "By right of birth
  and blood.

423
00:29:20.926 --> 00:29:24.010
 "I do this day lay claim
 to the Iron Throne
 of Westeros.

424
00:29:24.079 --> 00:29:26.680
 "Let all true men
 declare their loyalty."

425
00:29:26.748 --> 00:29:29.048
    When Eddard Stark learned
    the truth. he told only me.

426
00:29:29.117 --> 00:29:31.351
            I'll not make
            the same mistake.

427
00:29:31.420 --> 00:29:33.470
  Send copies of that letter
  to every corner of the realm.

428
00:29:33.538 --> 00:29:35.455
    from the Arbor to the Wall.

429
00:29:35.524 --> 00:29:38.392
         The time has
         come to choose.

430
00:29:38.460 --> 00:29:40.860
    Let no man claim
    ignorance as an excuse.

431
00:29:40.929 --> 00:29:43.463
 Your Grace.
 the Lannisters
 are the true enemy.

432
00:29:43.532 --> 00:29:45.632
 If. for the time being.
 you could make peace
 with your brother...

433
00:29:45.700 --> 00:29:47.801
            I'll not make peace
            with Renly while he
            calls himself king.

434
00:29:47.870 --> 00:29:49.670
 Well. many have
 already declared for him.

435
00:29:49.738 --> 00:29:51.972
   Mace Tyrell.
   Randyll Tarly.

436
00:29:52.041 --> 00:29:55.242
         Stannis does not need
         to beg this lord or
         that lord for support.

437
00:29:55.310 --> 00:29:57.210
             The Lord of Light
             stands behind him.

438
00:29:57.279 --> 00:30:00.180
   And how many ships
   has the Lord of Light
   got in his fleet?

439
00:30:00.249 --> 00:30:01.481
      He has no need for ships.

440
00:30:01.549 --> 00:30:02.715
 DAVOS:
 I'm sure he doesn't.

441
00:30:02.784 --> 00:30:04.784
 but we do if
 we're going to war.

442
00:30:04.853 --> 00:30:07.471
 If not Renly. Your Grace.
 join forces with Robb Stark.

443
00:30:07.539 --> 00:30:09.840
           Who would steal
           the northern half
           of my kingdom.

444
00:30:09.908 --> 00:30:13.159
   I've always served thieves
   according to their deserts.
   as you well know. Ser Davos.

445
00:30:13.229 --> 00:30:16.280
    Joffrey. Renly. Robb Stark.
    they're all thieves.

446
00:30:16.348 --> 00:30:19.549
          They'll bend the knee
          or I'll destroy them.

447
00:30:19.617 --> 00:30:22.552
          I owe you an apology.
          my king.

448
00:30:23.388 --> 00:30:25.388
           My duty is to serve.

449
00:30:25.457 --> 00:30:29.592
    You have chosen the new god
    over the old gods.

450
00:30:29.661 --> 00:30:33.063
          May the Lord of Light
          watch over us all.

451
00:30:33.131 --> 00:30:35.465
 Shall we drink together?

452
00:30:35.534 --> 00:30:37.467
      Don't.

453
00:30:37.536 --> 00:30:42.105
         A cup of wine to honor
         the one true god.

454
00:31:25.033 --> 00:31:26.032
                       (THUDS)

455
00:31:26.101 --> 00:31:27.117
        (MEN MURMURING)

456
00:31:28.487 --> 00:31:31.654
 The night is dark
 and full of terrors.
 old man.

457
00:31:31.724 --> 00:31:34.791
   but the fire
   burns them all away.

458
00:31:40.065 --> 00:31:42.182
           (CHATTER)

459
00:32:09.912 --> 00:32:11.811
       King in the North.

460
00:32:14.583 --> 00:32:18.317
    I keep expecting you
    to leave me in one castle
    or another for safekeeping.

461
00:32:18.386 --> 00:32:21.254
          but you drag me along
          from camp to camp.

462
00:32:22.908 --> 00:32:25.108
             Have you grown
             fond of me. Stark?

463
00:32:25.177 --> 00:32:27.010
                Is that it?

464
00:32:27.079 --> 00:32:29.913
            I've never seen you
            with a girl.

465
00:32:29.982 --> 00:32:32.482
  If I left you with
  one of my bannermen.

466
00:32:32.551 --> 00:32:35.552
 your father would know
 within a fortnight

467
00:32:35.620 --> 00:32:39.189
  and my bannerman
  would receive a raven
  with a message.

468
00:32:39.258 --> 00:32:42.792
  "Release my son
  and you'll be rich
  beyond your dreams.

469
00:32:42.861 --> 00:32:46.296
 "Refuse and your house
 will be destroyed.
 root and stem."

470
00:32:46.365 --> 00:32:50.900
    You don't trust the loyalty
    of the men following you
    into battle?

471
00:32:50.970 --> 00:32:53.003
 Oh. I trust them
 with my life.

472
00:32:54.440 --> 00:32:55.538
 just not with yours.

473
00:32:56.342 --> 00:32:58.342
                 Smart boy.

474
00:32:58.410 --> 00:33:00.143
               What's wrong?

475
00:33:00.212 --> 00:33:01.811
               Don't like being
               called "boy"?

476
00:33:03.015 --> 00:33:04.714
                 Insulted?

477
00:33:06.585 --> 00:33:08.151
      (GREY WIND SNARLING)

478
00:33:12.024 --> 00:33:14.757
 ROBB: You insult yourself.
 Kingslayer.

479
00:33:16.761 --> 00:33:18.061
 You've been
 defeated by a boy.

480
00:33:18.130 --> 00:33:19.997
       (HEAVY BREATHING)

481
00:33:20.065 --> 00:33:22.199
 You're held captive
 by a boy.

482
00:33:25.137 --> 00:33:26.903
 Perhaps you'll be
 killed by a boy.

483
00:33:33.979 --> 00:33:37.547
    Stannis Baratheon
    sent ravens to all the
    high lords of Westeros.

484
00:33:39.151 --> 00:33:42.685
 King Joffrey Baratheon
 is neither a true king

485
00:33:42.754 --> 00:33:45.906
 nor a true Baratheon.

486
00:33:45.974 --> 00:33:47.674
 He's your bastard son.

487
00:33:47.743 --> 00:33:50.109
                If that's true.
                Stannis is the
                rightful king.

488
00:33:50.178 --> 00:33:52.846
        How convenient for him.

489
00:33:52.915 --> 00:33:56.583
       My father learned
       the truth.

490
00:33:56.652 --> 00:33:58.284
 That's why you
 had him executed.

491
00:33:58.353 --> 00:34:00.620
            I was your prisoner
            when Ned Stark
            lost his head.

492
00:34:00.689 --> 00:34:04.357
 Your son killed him
 so the world wouldn't
 learn who fathered him.

493
00:34:04.426 --> 00:34:06.827
 And you.

494
00:34:06.895 --> 00:34:10.063
 you pushed my brother
 from a window because
 he saw you with the queen.

495
00:34:15.236 --> 00:34:18.538
              You have proof?

496
00:34:18.607 --> 00:34:21.074
         Or do you want
         to trade gossip like
         a couple of fishwives?

497
00:34:21.142 --> 00:34:25.011
 I'm sending one of
 your cousins down to King's
 Landing with my peace terms.

498
00:34:25.080 --> 00:34:28.348
           You think
           my father's going to
           negotiate with you?

499
00:34:28.416 --> 00:34:30.450
             You don't know him
             very well.

500
00:34:30.519 --> 00:34:35.054
 No. but he's starting
 to know me.

501
00:34:35.123 --> 00:34:38.424
          Three victories don't
          make you a conqueror.

502
00:34:39.828 --> 00:34:41.461
 It's better
 than three defeats.

503
00:34:50.372 --> 00:34:51.972
     (SNARLING)

504
00:35:11.109 --> 00:35:12.808
 SHAE: This city stinks.

505
00:35:16.080 --> 00:35:17.680
 Like dead bodies.

506
00:35:17.749 --> 00:35:19.816
            TYRION:
            A bit corpsey. yes.

507
00:35:20.686 --> 00:35:22.385
          And shit.

508
00:35:22.454 --> 00:35:24.036
           I thought you
           wanted to come here.

509
00:35:27.593 --> 00:35:29.959
          I love it.

510
00:35:30.028 --> 00:35:33.713
          You love the smell of
          dead bodies and shit?

511
00:35:33.782 --> 00:35:36.699
 And cum and garlic and rum.

512
00:35:36.768 --> 00:35:39.970
              You can smell cum
              from the balcony?

513
00:35:40.038 --> 00:35:43.340
   I love the stink.
   I love the noise.

514
00:35:43.408 --> 00:35:45.408
     Cities make me
     want to fuck.

515
00:35:46.378 --> 00:35:48.577
        And so did the country.

516
00:35:50.265 --> 00:35:51.731
              (SIGHS)

517
00:35:51.800 --> 00:35:53.300
     This is where I belong.

518
00:35:53.368 --> 00:35:56.202
 Yes. well.
 you need to be careful.

519
00:35:56.271 --> 00:35:57.803
  No one can know
  you're here.

520
00:35:57.872 --> 00:35:59.489
        No one will know.

521
00:35:59.558 --> 00:36:01.274
 You can't trust anyone
 in King's Landing.

522
00:36:01.359 --> 00:36:04.361
 They're all liars.
 good liars. bad liars.

523
00:36:04.429 --> 00:36:06.863
 one or two great liars.

524
00:36:06.931 --> 00:36:08.798
                What about you?

525
00:36:08.867 --> 00:36:11.634
 Me? I'm not from here.
 I'm a slave to the truth.

526
00:36:13.305 --> 00:36:14.353
           (LAUGHS) Truth?

527
00:36:16.324 --> 00:36:19.358
            You are the biggest
            little liar I have
            ever met.

528
00:36:19.427 --> 00:36:21.393
 Why do you think
 I am so little?

529
00:36:21.463 --> 00:36:25.782
 I'm being crushed beneath
 the weight of all that truth.

530
00:36:30.222 --> 00:36:32.989
        Ned Stark
        actually slept on this.

531
00:36:33.058 --> 00:36:36.692
          As if the poor man
          didn't suffer enough.

532
00:36:38.629 --> 00:36:42.098
        One of the many changes
        we'll have to make
        around here.

533
00:36:53.261 --> 00:36:55.228
     Lord Baelish.

534
00:36:55.297 --> 00:36:56.629
 Your Grace.

535
00:36:56.698 --> 00:36:59.098
   I wonder if I might
   ask you for a favor.

536
00:36:59.167 --> 00:37:00.700
 Of course. Your Grace.

537
00:37:00.768 --> 00:37:02.735
   Ned Stark's
   youngest daughter Arya.

538
00:37:02.804 --> 00:37:05.538
     we can't seem
     to locate her.

539
00:37:05.607 --> 00:37:09.609
 If she's escaped the capital.
 Winterfell seems
 the logical destination.

540
00:37:09.677 --> 00:37:12.112
            And yet my friends
            in the North report
            no sign of her.

541
00:37:12.180 --> 00:37:14.080
         Curious.

542
00:37:14.149 --> 00:37:16.249
             If we choose
             to negotiate
             with the Starks.

543
00:37:16.318 --> 00:37:18.318
       the girl has some value.
       Whoever finds her...

544
00:37:18.387 --> 00:37:20.653
          Well. you know
          what they say about
          Lannisters and debts.

545
00:37:20.722 --> 00:37:23.089
 Well. you could ask
 Varys where she is.

546
00:37:24.192 --> 00:37:25.475
 He'll have
 an answer for you.

547
00:37:25.527 --> 00:37:26.993
 Whether you believe it...

548
00:37:27.061 --> 00:37:31.030
 Myself. I have always
 had a hard time
 trusting eunuchs.

549
00:37:31.098 --> 00:37:33.616
 Who knows what they want?

550
00:37:33.669 --> 00:37:35.568
                 A mockingbird.

551
00:37:36.872 --> 00:37:38.638
    You created your own sigil.
    didn't you?

552
00:37:38.707 --> 00:37:40.373
 Yes.

553
00:37:40.442 --> 00:37:44.410
    Appropriate.
    for a self-made man
    with so many songs to sing.

554
00:37:44.496 --> 00:37:46.095
  I'm glad you like it.

555
00:37:46.164 --> 00:37:48.130
     Some people are
     fortunate enough

556
00:37:48.199 --> 00:37:49.666
     to be born into
     the right family.

557
00:37:49.734 --> 00:37:52.151
    Others have to
    find their own way.

558
00:37:53.739 --> 00:37:55.772
            I heard a song once

559
00:37:55.840 --> 00:37:58.475
                about a boy
                of modest means

560
00:37:58.543 --> 00:38:01.027
       who found his way
       into the home of
       a very prominent family.

561
00:38:02.380 --> 00:38:03.996
           He loved
           the eldest daughter.

562
00:38:04.065 --> 00:38:07.750
            Sadly. she had eyes
            for another.

563
00:38:07.819 --> 00:38:12.555
 When boys and girls
 live in the same home.
 awkward situations can arise.

564
00:38:12.624 --> 00:38:17.710
 Sometimes. I've heard.
 even brothers and sisters
 develop certain affections.

565
00:38:17.779 --> 00:38:20.213
 And when those affections
 become common knowledge.

566
00:38:20.281 --> 00:38:24.133
 well. that is an awkward
 situation indeed.

567
00:38:24.202 --> 00:38:26.369
 especially in
 a prominent family.

568
00:38:26.437 --> 00:38:28.687
 But prominent families
 often forget a simple truth.

569
00:38:29.708 --> 00:38:31.173
    I've found.

570
00:38:32.260 --> 00:38:34.276
       And which truth is that?

571
00:38:34.346 --> 00:38:36.680
 Knowledge is power.

572
00:38:40.201 --> 00:38:42.485
                  Seize him.

573
00:38:44.439 --> 00:38:46.255
           Cut his throat.

574
00:38:46.925 --> 00:38:50.026
                    Stop. Wait.

575
00:38:50.095 --> 00:38:52.261
          I've changed my mind.
          Let him go.

576
00:38:55.300 --> 00:38:56.916
         Step back three paces.

577
00:38:58.486 --> 00:39:00.119
      Turn around.

578
00:39:00.922 --> 00:39:02.322
    Close your eyes.

579
00:39:06.712 --> 00:39:08.277
           Power is power.

580
00:39:10.898 --> 00:39:14.667
     Do see if you can
     take some time away from
     your coins and your whores

581
00:39:14.735 --> 00:39:16.602
         to locate
         the Stark girl for me.

582
00:39:16.671 --> 00:39:19.339
              I would very much
              appreciate it.

583
00:39:30.068 --> 00:39:32.685
           ROBB: You're
           Ser Alton Lannister?

584
00:39:32.754 --> 00:39:34.787
   I am. Your Grace.

585
00:39:34.856 --> 00:39:38.291
   ROBB: I offer your cousins
   peace if they meet my terms.

586
00:39:38.359 --> 00:39:43.229
       First. your family
       must release my sisters.

587
00:39:43.298 --> 00:39:46.266
      Second. my father's bones
      must be returned to us

588
00:39:46.334 --> 00:39:48.635
         so he may rest beside
         his brother and sister

589
00:39:48.703 --> 00:39:51.037
            in the crypts
            beneath Winterfell.

590
00:39:51.122 --> 00:39:55.558
   And the remains of all those
   who died in his service
   must also be returned.

591
00:39:55.627 --> 00:39:58.111
          Their families
          can honor them
          with proper funerals.

592
00:39:58.179 --> 00:39:59.845
    An honorable request.
    Your Grace.

593
00:39:59.914 --> 00:40:02.748
                       Third...

594
00:40:02.817 --> 00:40:07.887
   Joffrey and the Queen Regent
   must renounce all claim to
   dominion of the North.

595
00:40:07.955 --> 00:40:10.123
          From this time
          till the end of time.

596
00:40:10.191 --> 00:40:12.658
           we are a free and
           independent kingdom.

597
00:40:12.727 --> 00:40:14.760
 The King in the North.

598
00:40:14.829 --> 00:40:17.230
             King in the North.
           King in the North.

599
00:40:17.298 --> 00:40:21.034
      Neither Joffrey nor any
      of his men shall set foot
      in our lands again.

600
00:40:21.102 --> 00:40:23.136
               If he disregards
               this command.

601
00:40:23.205 --> 00:40:26.605
                he shall suffer
                the same fate
                as my father.

602
00:40:26.674 --> 00:40:30.944
    only I don't need a servant
    to do my beheading for me.

603
00:40:31.012 --> 00:40:34.380
 These are...
 Your Grace. these are...

604
00:40:34.448 --> 00:40:36.983
          These are my terms.

605
00:40:37.051 --> 00:40:40.152
       If the Queen Regent
       and her son meet them.
       I'll give them peace.

606
00:40:40.221 --> 00:40:41.487
             If not.

607
00:40:43.290 --> 00:40:45.758
    I will litter the South
    with Lannister dead.

608
00:40:45.827 --> 00:40:48.561
    King Joffrey
    is a Baratheon.
    Your Grace.

609
00:40:48.647 --> 00:40:50.212
        Oh. is he?

610
00:40:51.649 --> 00:40:54.984
       You'll ride at daybreak.
       Ser Alton.

611
00:40:55.036 --> 00:40:57.436
             That will be all
             for tonight.

612
00:41:12.420 --> 00:41:14.437
            A word. Your Grace?

613
00:41:16.341 --> 00:41:19.008
 You don't have to
 call me "Your Grace"
 when no one's around.

614
00:41:19.076 --> 00:41:21.727
       It's not so bad
       once you get used to it.

615
00:41:21.796 --> 00:41:24.647
  I'm glad someone's
  gotten used to it.

616
00:41:24.716 --> 00:41:26.915
       The Lannisters are going
       to reject your terms.
       you know?

617
00:41:26.985 --> 00:41:28.852
 Of course they are.

618
00:41:28.920 --> 00:41:31.220
           We can fight them
           in the fields
           as long as you like.

619
00:41:31.288 --> 00:41:34.557
         but we won't beat them
         until you take
         King's Landing.

620
00:41:36.427 --> 00:41:39.629
              And we can't take
              King's Landing
              without ships.

621
00:41:39.697 --> 00:41:42.164
            My father has ships
            and men who know
            how to sail them.

622
00:41:42.233 --> 00:41:44.016
 Men who fought my father.

623
00:41:44.085 --> 00:41:46.351
     Men who fought King Robert
     to free themselves

624
00:41:46.420 --> 00:41:50.073
    from the yoke of the South.
    just like you're doing now.

625
00:41:51.476 --> 00:41:53.442
                   I'm his only
                   living son.

626
00:41:54.579 --> 00:41:57.547
            He'll listen to me.
            I know he will.

627
00:42:00.101 --> 00:42:03.369
              I'm not a Stark.
              I know that.

628
00:42:03.438 --> 00:42:06.256
      But your father raised me
      to be an honorable man.

629
00:42:08.276 --> 00:42:10.576
              We can avenge him
              together.

630
00:42:12.731 --> 00:42:14.931
                 You don't want
                 Balon Greyjoy
                 for an ally.

631
00:42:15.000 --> 00:42:17.299
 I need his ships.
 They say he has 200.

632
00:42:17.368 --> 00:42:21.270
        They say a million rats
        live in the sewers
        of King's Landing.

633
00:42:21.339 --> 00:42:22.839
           Shall we rally them
           to fight for us?

634
00:42:22.908 --> 00:42:24.807
 I understand
 you don't trust
 Lord Greyjoy.

635
00:42:24.876 --> 00:42:29.478
         I don't trust
         Lord Greyjoy because
         he is not trustworthy.

636
00:42:29.548 --> 00:42:32.048
             Your father had
             to go to war to
             end his rebellion.

637
00:42:32.116 --> 00:42:35.919
  Yes. And now
  I'm the one rebelling
  against the throne.

638
00:42:35.987 --> 00:42:38.254
 Before me. it was Father.

639
00:42:38.322 --> 00:42:40.339
  You married one rebel
  and mothered another.

640
00:42:40.408 --> 00:42:42.975
              I mothered more
              than just rebels.

641
00:42:43.044 --> 00:42:45.295
             a fact you seem
             to have forgotten.

642
00:42:45.347 --> 00:42:47.613
 If I trade the Kingslayer
 for two girls.

643
00:42:47.682 --> 00:42:49.615
 my bannermen will
 string me up by my feet.

644
00:42:49.684 --> 00:42:52.918
        You want to leave Sansa
        in the queen's hands?

645
00:42:52.988 --> 00:42:55.004
                    And Arya...

646
00:42:55.073 --> 00:42:58.307
      I haven't heard
      a word about Arya.

647
00:42:58.376 --> 00:42:59.842
     What are we fighting for.
     if not for them?

648
00:42:59.911 --> 00:43:03.446
    It's more
    complicated than that!
    You know it is.

649
00:43:18.079 --> 00:43:21.680
               It's time for me
               to go home.

650
00:43:21.749 --> 00:43:25.451
           I haven't seen Bran
           or Rickon in months.

651
00:43:25.520 --> 00:43:27.803
       You can't go
       to Winterfell.

652
00:43:28.806 --> 00:43:30.306
             I beg your pardon?

653
00:43:30.374 --> 00:43:33.609
    I'll send Rodrik to
    watch over the boys

654
00:43:33.678 --> 00:43:38.081
     because tomorrow
     you'll ride south
     to the Stormlands.

655
00:43:38.149 --> 00:43:40.183
             Why in the name
             of all the gods...

656
00:43:40.251 --> 00:43:44.053
    Because I need you
    to negotiate with
    Renly Baratheon.

657
00:43:44.122 --> 00:43:46.221
    He's rallied
    an army of 100.000.

658
00:43:46.290 --> 00:43:48.057
 You know him.
 You know his family.

659
00:43:48.126 --> 00:43:50.526
        I haven't seen
        Renly Baratheon
        since he was a boy.

660
00:43:50.594 --> 00:43:51.894
             You have a hundred
             other lords...

661
00:43:51.963 --> 00:43:54.964
 Which of these lords
 do I trust more than you?

662
00:43:55.867 --> 00:43:58.701
 If Renly sides with us.

663
00:43:58.769 --> 00:44:01.270
 we'll outnumber them
 two to one.

664
00:44:01.339 --> 00:44:04.173
  When they feel the jaws
  beginning to shut.
  they'll sue for peace.

665
00:44:04.242 --> 00:44:06.909
 We'll get the girls back.

666
00:44:06.978 --> 00:44:09.879
 Then we'll all go home.
 for good.

667
00:44:18.522 --> 00:44:20.289
             I will ride
             at first light.

668
00:44:29.200 --> 00:44:32.301
 We will all be together
 again soon. I promise.

669
00:44:37.842 --> 00:44:40.309
           You've done so well.

670
00:44:41.780 --> 00:44:44.513
            Your father
            would be proud.

671
00:44:53.591 --> 00:44:54.957
 Give Lord Renly my regards.

672
00:44:55.026 --> 00:44:56.359
               King Renly.

673
00:44:57.662 --> 00:45:00.163
           There's a king
           in every corner now.

674
00:45:13.394 --> 00:45:15.828
             What is all this?

675
00:45:15.897 --> 00:45:18.230
 Returning this room to
 its proper appearance.

676
00:45:18.299 --> 00:45:21.167
 Say what you will
 about the Targaryens.
 they were conquerors.

677
00:45:21.235 --> 00:45:23.903
               That is a seat
               for a conqueror.

678
00:45:23.971 --> 00:45:27.572
   It needs a room to match it.
   not vines and flowers.

679
00:45:27.641 --> 00:45:30.042
 We can't find Arya Stark.

680
00:45:30.111 --> 00:45:32.144
          With luck. she's dead
          in a ditch somewhere.

681
00:45:32.213 --> 00:45:34.280
 Perhaps.
 But if not. we need her.

682
00:45:34.348 --> 00:45:36.615
 They'll never give
 Jaime back to us
 for Sansa alone.

683
00:45:36.684 --> 00:45:39.185
            I think they might.
            They're weak.

684
00:45:39.253 --> 00:45:41.838
        They put too much value
        on their women.

685
00:45:41.906 --> 00:45:44.941
  We need to set our armies
  to the task of finding her.

686
00:45:45.009 --> 00:45:46.976
          Send out as many men
          as we can.

687
00:45:47.045 --> 00:45:48.911
  I'm sure if you
  asked Grandfather...

688
00:45:48.980 --> 00:45:52.731
         The king does not ask.
         he commands.

689
00:45:52.800 --> 00:45:55.651
         And my grandfather's
         stupidity in the field
         of battle

690
00:45:55.719 --> 00:45:58.553
       is the reason Robb Stark
       has Uncle Jaime
       in the first place.

691
00:45:58.622 --> 00:46:00.489
 His life is in danger.

692
00:46:01.425 --> 00:46:03.058
                  We're at war.

693
00:46:03.127 --> 00:46:05.261
                 All our lives
                 are in danger.

694
00:46:09.217 --> 00:46:11.917
       I heard a disgusting lie
       about Uncle Jaime.

695
00:46:12.753 --> 00:46:15.321
                    And you.

696
00:46:15.390 --> 00:46:19.041
 Our enemies will say
 anything to weaken
 your claim to the throne.

697
00:46:19.109 --> 00:46:20.959
            It's not a claim.
            The throne is mine.

698
00:46:22.730 --> 00:46:24.363
 Of course it is.

699
00:46:26.417 --> 00:46:28.484
   No one believes
   this foul gossip.

700
00:46:28.552 --> 00:46:30.552
           Someone believes it.

701
00:46:32.090 --> 00:46:34.556
                Father had
                other children?

702
00:46:34.625 --> 00:46:36.942
          Besides me and Tommen
          and Myrcella?

703
00:46:37.010 --> 00:46:38.544
 (HAMMERS CLATTERING)

704
00:46:39.380 --> 00:46:41.229
 What are you asking?

705
00:46:41.298 --> 00:46:44.250
     I'm asking
     if he fucked other women
     when he grew tired of you.

706
00:46:44.335 --> 00:46:46.669
        How many bastards
        does he have running...

707
00:46:47.338 --> 00:46:48.838
          (WORK STOPS)

708
00:47:02.620 --> 00:47:06.705
        What you just did
        is punishable by death.

709
00:47:10.060 --> 00:47:12.327
    You will never do it again.

710
00:47:12.997 --> 00:47:14.663
                   Never.

711
00:47:20.788 --> 00:47:22.788
 That will be all. Mother.

712
00:47:27.428 --> 00:47:29.595
                (SCREAMING)

713
00:47:29.664 --> 00:47:31.631
 No. no. no. no.

714
00:47:31.699 --> 00:47:34.533
 Do you have any idea
 how ridiculous you sound?

715
00:47:34.602 --> 00:47:36.052
   Ease into it.

716
00:47:36.120 --> 00:47:39.121
 Slowly. with passion.

717
00:47:41.426 --> 00:47:42.741
               Oh. yeah.

718
00:47:44.011 --> 00:47:46.778
 Go wash yourselves.
 Put some clothes on.

719
00:47:46.847 --> 00:47:49.348
 Both of you are
 working tonight.

720
00:47:53.287 --> 00:47:55.187
       We do things
       differently here. Daisy.

721
00:47:55.256 --> 00:47:59.158
        This isn't some
        five-copper bawdy house
        in Hayseed Hall.

722
00:47:59.227 --> 00:48:01.827
    Haystack Hall.
       Wherever you're from.

723
00:48:01.895 --> 00:48:06.398
       Our establishment
       doesn't cater to plowmen
       and goat herders.

724
00:48:06.467 --> 00:48:08.200
                    Lord Olsen.

725
00:48:08.269 --> 00:48:10.236
      Taste is everything here.

726
00:48:10.304 --> 00:48:12.238
           Littlefinger's
           a fancy man.

727
00:48:12.306 --> 00:48:13.939
                 Don't call him
                 Littlefinger.

728
00:48:14.008 --> 00:48:15.457
            He doesn't like it.

729
00:48:15.509 --> 00:48:17.843
 Lord Baelish.

730
00:48:23.684 --> 00:48:25.684
 She pretends she doesn't
 speak the common tongue

731
00:48:25.753 --> 00:48:28.354
   so that people will
   think she's exotic.

732
00:48:28.422 --> 00:48:31.257
 She grew up
 just down the road
 in Flea Bottom.

733
00:48:31.325 --> 00:48:33.809
               She's beautiful.

734
00:48:33.877 --> 00:48:37.713
 She's a dumb slut. really.
 but a lid for every pot.

735
00:48:37.781 --> 00:48:39.348
               (ARMOR RATTLING)

736
00:48:42.253 --> 00:48:44.553
                Lord Commander.

737
00:48:44.622 --> 00:48:47.456
         Good to see you again.

738
00:48:52.597 --> 00:48:53.612
 (SNAPS FINGERS)

739
00:49:01.239 --> 00:49:02.821
              (DOOR BREAKS)
                (PEOPLE SCREAM)

740
00:49:02.890 --> 00:49:06.525
         You do realize this
         establishment is owned
         by Lord Petyr Baelish.

741
00:49:06.593 --> 00:49:08.793
                the King's
                Master of Coin.

742
00:49:08.862 --> 00:49:10.663
               Coin which goes
               in many pockets.

743
00:49:11.199 --> 00:49:12.281
        Orders.

744
00:49:12.349 --> 00:49:13.582
               Whose orders?

745
00:49:13.651 --> 00:49:16.234
 Someone who doesn't care
 what Littlefinger thinks.

746
00:49:17.337 --> 00:49:18.336
          (WOMAN SOBBING)

747
00:49:23.327 --> 00:49:24.960
      (BABY CRYING)

748
00:49:34.154 --> 00:49:37.122
     No. you can't.
     No! Please!

749
00:49:37.942 --> 00:49:40.376
           No! Not my Barra!

750
00:49:40.428 --> 00:49:42.678
 Please. Please.

751
00:49:42.747 --> 00:49:43.862
           Enough. Get it done.

752
00:49:43.931 --> 00:49:45.831
              Kill the bastard.
 WOMAN: No. no!

753
00:49:45.900 --> 00:49:48.300
 Please.
                  Give it here.

754
00:49:48.386 --> 00:49:51.387
 No. please.

755
00:49:51.456 --> 00:49:52.938
               (DAGGER SLASHES)
             (SCREAMS)

756
00:50:00.948 --> 00:50:03.248
            MAN: Spread out.
            Search every house.

757
00:50:03.317 --> 00:50:05.584
            Every room.
            Look in every room.

758
00:50:07.855 --> 00:50:09.088
                     (GRUNTING)

759
00:50:11.609 --> 00:50:12.891
       (WOMEN SCREAMING)

760
00:50:19.533 --> 00:50:21.333
       (PEOPLE SHOUTING)

761
00:50:30.261 --> 00:50:32.728
         Gendry!
         His name is Gendry.

762
00:50:32.796 --> 00:50:34.529
      Where is the bastard?

763
00:50:34.598 --> 00:50:37.199
 The Night's Watch!
 Please. stop!

764
00:50:37.268 --> 00:50:38.784
              Where?

765
00:50:38.853 --> 00:50:41.720
         They took him
         up the Kingsroad.
         heading north.

766
00:50:41.788 --> 00:50:43.038
          How will we know him?

767
00:50:43.107 --> 00:50:45.390
 He's got
 a bull's head helmet.

768
00:50:45.459 --> 00:50:46.859
 He made it himself.

769
00:50:46.927 --> 00:50:48.226
                  Find him.
